        "hunk_index": 3,
        "change_category": "bug_fix",
        "intent_summary": "Initialize mdb_n_entries count for VLAN-specific multicast groups during port context initialization",
        "what": "Added a conditional block in br_multicast_port_ctx_init that acquires multicast_lock, counts existing multicast groups matching a specific VLAN ID, and assigns the result to pmctx->mdb_n_entries.",
        "how": "Ensures the multicast database entry count is accurately initialized for VLAN-aware bridge ports during context setup, protecting the operation with spinlocks to prevent race conditions."
      }
    },
    {
      "intent_record": {
        "hunk_index": 4,
        "change_category": "bug_fix",
        "intent_summary": "Removed obsolete VLAN multicast group counter refresh logic from __br_multicast_enable_port_ctx after the underlying counter accuracy issue was resolved elsewhere.",
        "what": "Removed a conditional code block that checked if the port context is VLAN-related, then iterated through multicast groups to count entries matching the VLAN ID and updated the mdb_n_entries counter using WRITE_ONCE.",
        "how": "Eliminates the manual refresh of the mdb_n_entries counter when enabling a port context for VLANs. The counter will no longer be recalculated during port context enablement, relying instead on other mechanisms to maintain accurate group counts."
      }
